{"text": "BACKGROUND\n\n| grew up on a small farm and I know the\nvalue and results of hard work and\nsacrifice. | had the unfortunate experience\nof losing both of my parents at very\nyoung ages, and | know what it's like to\nfeel desperate and alone. | relied on\nstudent loans to help get myself through\nschool and from this | have become a\nstrong advocate for fairness\nwholeheartedly believe in the ideals of\nour Country and the continuous need to\nstrive to meet them. | believe in the US.\nConstitution and the freedoms it bestows\nand | believe everyone deserves respect\nand the assumption of being good. | work\nhard, and play harder, and | have the\nextreme ability to find good in the most\n\ntroubled of situations.\n\nCONTACT\n\nPHONE:\n774-293-8472\n\nWEBSITE:\nTracyforCongress.com\n\nEMA\nfracy@ tracyforcongress.com\n\nPILLARS\nC-ountry\nL-eadership\nA-ccomplishment\nS-acrifice\nS-ervice\n\nTRACY LYN LOVVORN\n\nRepublican Candidate\nMA- Congressional District 2\nWife, Mother, Healthcare Provider, Operational Manager, Small\nBusiness Owner, Advocate, Outdoor/Nature /Animal Lover\n\nEDUCATION\n\nDoctor of Physical Therapy University Of Montana, Missoula, MT\nJan 2020 - Current\n\u2018Master of Physical Therapy Mount St. Mary's University, Los Angeles\n\u2018Aug. 1995 ~ Dec. 1997\nB.S. Exercise Physiology / Kinesiology San Diego State Univ.\n\u2018Aug. 1991 - June 1995\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\n2018 Republican Candidate MA- Congressional District 2.\n\u2018As @ political outsider and relative unknown, I won the Republican Primary\neaming 61% of the vote. As a moderate fiscally conservative republican, |\nran the most successful and cost-effective campaign of all MA\ncongressional republican candidates, receiving 33% of the vote while\nbeing outspent 37-1 by a 22yr incumbent.\n\nCEO Evolution Therapeutics, LLC North Gratton, MA\n(Owner operator Evolution Physical Therapy. Outpatient Orthopedics.\nAfter my case settled, (see below) | was in essence black balled from my\nindustry making it extremely difficult to find @ comparable job in my field.\nbecame a practicing clinician again and worked throughout Worcester\nCounty providing physical therapy to individuals in their homes. I then\n\u2018opened my own Private Practice Cinic, in my current hometown, and |\nhave been loving every minute of providing care to my local community\n\nRegional Rehab Director/Manager Clinical, Operations, & Medicare\n\u2018Compliance\n20+ years working and growing professionally in the Skiled Nursing and\nRehabilitation environment with various companies across the United\nStates, Professional career path from staff clinician to corporate level,\nclinical, operational, and compliance management\n\nSIGNIFICANT ACHIEVEMENTS\n\n2009-2014 \u201cUnited States ex rel. Lovvorn v. EHSI, et. al. C.A. 10-1580 (E.D.\nPa) Working in support of the Office of the Inspector General, AG Holder,\nDept of Health and Human Services, and Assistant USAG office of PA, |\nstood up for thousands of sick, elderly, and frail senior citizens in multiple\nskilled nursing facilities. | worked to fight coruption, waste, fraud and\nabuse. My case set a precedent that has worked fo SAVE fax payers\u2019\n\u2018money and has resulted in 100's of millions of dollars being returned to the\nMedicare Trust Fund. It also forced a change in the methods that rehab is\nbilled in the skied nursing environment, protecting patients and helping to\nensure quality care,\n\nHold PT License in the States of: MA, MD, PA, NC, CA\nCertified Federal Medicare Surveyor- AAASF Certification\nCHC- Certification in Healthcare Compliance\nIAABO- Certified Official (Intemational Association of Approved Basketball\nOfficials)",
